  "prefLabel": "Jus 1505.01 Delegation of Authority to Assistant County Attorneys",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Jus 1505.01 Delegation of Authority to Assistant County Attorneys. Pursuant to RSA 7:6-b, III, a county attorney shall have the authority to delegate to any assistant county attorney within the county the authority to issue written demands pursuant to RSA 7:6-b.\n\nSource. #8082, eff 5-8-04",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/jus1500.html"
